  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10c-catfishes-remaining-catfish-from-south-america/ageneiosus_vittatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Slopehead catfish of the genus Ageneiosus are particularly noticeable for their strongly flattened head. These predators can reach an overall length of 30 cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10c-catfishes-remaining-catfish-from-south-america/ageneiosus_vittatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Origin: Peru. Ageneiosus vittatus was imported from Peru for the first time in July 2002.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10c-catfishes-remaining-catfish-from-south-america/ageneiosus_vittatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Large tanks are necessary for keeping this species.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10c-catfishes-remaining-catfish-from-south-america/ageneiosus_vittatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>A dark bottom, some stones and bogwood should be used for the tank layout. A large filtration unit is important for water quality, which is the most basic point for the successful keeping of this species.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10c-catfishes-remaining-catfish-from-south-america/ageneiosus_vittatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>In their habitat they are pure carnivores, which should be considered before acquiring them. It is best to give them live food; after habituation they will eat fish meat, earthworms or shrimps.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10c-catfishes-remaining-catfish-from-south-america/ageneiosus_vittatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>With sufficient feeding and good water quality breeding is possible, but usually not very productive due to the fragility of the larvae.</p>"
    }
  ],
